{"createdAt":"2026-09-30T12:11:11.466Z","data":{"body":[{"_key":"p2","_type":"image","alt":"Image from Gyazo","asset":{"_ref":"01M3TNWQ51J8P14CSK2Q7P1C7V","_type":"reference","url":"../../media/4b23cb787c6d48925d3440c28610bfceee1b4f9ddc7a4ab5cf80011ef824b2bc.png"},"height":1890,"link":{"href":"../../media/4b23cb787c6d48925d3440c28610bfceee1b4f9ddc7a4ab5cf80011ef824b2bc.png"},"width":2142},{"_key":"p2-g1","_type":"poc_markdown","body":"&#xA;Obsidian is way too useful."},{"_key":"p4","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"p3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"What is Obsidian?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"p5","_type":"poc_markdown","body":"- The basic features are the same as Notion, and you write using [Markdown](/en/tech/markdown/)\n- Notion stores data in a hierarchical manner, while Obsidian structures data through links between notes, etc.\n- To be frank, Notion has more features, but Obsidian runs locally and is noticeably lighter than Notion\n  - It was perfect for me, since I couldn’t fully take advantage of Notion’s features and wanted certain features or an API\n- You can control appearance and behavior with community-developed themes and plugins"}],"date_precision":"day","description":"I also write this blog in Obsidian.","emoji":"🪨","hidden_from_listing":false,"is_work_in_progress":true,"properties":{},"published_updated_at":"2025-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","title":"Isn't Obsidian way too useful?","translation":{"automatic":true,"sourceId":"01M3S3KM7DGHTZ9V5ADDDJVG8V"}},"id":"01M3S3KN7ACT9JZH5S4X0BP1W3","locale":"en","publishedAt":"2025-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","seo":{"canonical":null,"description":null,"image":null,"noIndex":false,"title":null},"slug":"obsidian","terms":{"category":[{"id":"01M40J9EZG7N7XMZG3TAFYBE98","label":"Miscellaneous","locale":"en","name":"category","parentId":null,"slug":"misc","translationGroup":"01M40J9EZG7N7XMZG3TAFYBE98"}],"tag":[{"id":"01M40J9Q9ZTBA6GQGRV3E9D2YK","label":"dev","locale":"en","name":"tag","parentId":null,"slug":"